  <div class="wrap">
<div class="hub-sub">Extended reference poster · Chinese GAAP (ASBE / CAS) · 生物资产 · Cost model is the default — the presumption is REVERSED relative to IAS 41 · RMB examples</div></div></div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Living animals and plants, measured predominantly at cost</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 5 governs LIVING animals and PLANTS held by an enterprise — the Chinese COUNTERPART to IAS 41 (Agriculture) internationally. THE most STRIKING feature of this Standard is that it REVERSES the international PRESUMPTION: WHERE IAS 41 REQUIRES fair value MEASUREMENT as the DEFAULT (with cost ONLY as a fallback), ASBE No. 5 makes COST the DEFAULT, PERMITTING fair value ONLY in NARROW, RESTRICTED circumstances (Section 6) — one of the MOST significant MEASUREMENT divergences ANYWHERE in the ASBE suite.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — Three Categories of Biological Assets</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Consumable, productive, and public welfare biological assets</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Category</span><span>Description</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Consumable biological assets</span><span>Held for EVENTUAL sale or harvest (e.g. CROPS, livestock RAISED for slaughter)</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Productive biological assets</span><span>Held to PRODUCE agricultural PRODUCE, or for RENTAL, on a REPEATED or CONTINUOUS basis (e.g. FRUIT trees, DAIRY cattle)</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Public welfare biological assets</span><span>Held PRIMARILY for environmental PROTECTION purposes (e.g. WINDBREAK or WATER-conservation forests)</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Consumable Biological Assets</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Held for eventual sale or harvest</div><div class="text-supporting">CONSUMABLE biological ASSETS — CROPS, VEGETABLES, and LIVESTOCK raised for SLAUGHTER — are MEASURED at COST, ACCUMULATING expenditure UNTIL harvest or SALE, at WHICH point they TRANSFER into INVENTORY (governed by ASBE No. 1).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Productive Biological Assets</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Depreciated like fixed assets, over their productive life</div><div class="text-supporting">PRODUCTIVE biological ASSETS — FRUIT-bearing TREES, DAIRY cattle, RUBBER trees — are MEASURED at COST LESS accumulated DEPRECIATION and IMPAIRMENT, SYSTEMATICALLY depreciated OVER their PRODUCTIVE useful LIFE, CONSISTENT with the SAME general APPROACH applied to FIXED assets under ASBE No. 4.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Public Welfare Biological Assets</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Environmental protection assets, measured at cost</div><div class="text-supporting">PUBLIC WELFARE biological ASSETS — held PRIMARILY for ENVIRONMENTAL or ECOLOGICAL protection PURPOSES RATHER than commercial PRODUCTION — are ALSO measured at COST, REFLECTING their FUNDAMENTALLY non-commercial NATURE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>THE KEY DIVERGENCE — Cost Is the Default, Not Fair Value</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A reversed presumption relative to IAS 41</div><div class="text-supporting">IAS 41 REQUIRES biological ASSETS to be MEASURED at FAIR VALUE LESS costs to SELL as the DEFAULT approach INTERNATIONALLY, PERMITTING cost ONLY as a NARROW FALLBACK where FAIR value CANNOT be MEASURED reliably. ASBE No. 5 TAKES the OPPOSITE starting POINT: COST is the DEFAULT measurement BASIS for ALL three categories of BIOLOGICAL asset, WITH the FAIR VALUE model PERMITTED ONLY where THERE is CLEAR evidence of an ACTIVE market PROVIDING reliable PRICE information (Section 7) — a GENUINELY significant, WELL-KNOWN REVERSAL of the international PRESUMPTION.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>When the Fair Value Model Is Permitted</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A narrow exception, mirroring the Investment Property restriction</div><div class="text-supporting">CONSISTENT with the SAME restrictive APPROACH seen in ASBE No. 3 (Investment Property — see the COMPANION poster), the FAIR VALUE model MAY be ELECTED for biological ASSETS ONLY where THERE is CONVINCING evidence of an ACTIVE, LIQUID market PROVIDING reliable, OBSERVABLE prices — a CONDITION that, in PRACTICE, is MET only for a NARROW range of Chinese AGRICULTURAL commodities with GENUINELY transparent SPOT markets.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Why ASBE Reverses IAS 41's Presumption</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">The same recurring caution around unreliable fair value estimates</div><div class="text-supporting">This REVERSAL reflects the SAME broader, RECURRING theme SEEN throughout the ASBE ASSET standards — a GENERAL scepticism TOWARD fair VALUE measurement WHERE reliable market EVIDENCE cannot be CONFIDENTLY established across China's DIVERSE, UNEVENLY developed AGRICULTURAL and commodity MARKETS. RATHER than REQUIRING preparers to ESTIMATE fair value WHERE genuinely reliable DATA may not EXIST (as IAS 41's DEFAULT approach WOULD require), ASBE PRIORITISES the VERIFIABILITY of historical COST, PERMITTING fair VALUE only WHERE its RELIABILITY is GENUINELY beyond QUESTION.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Cost-Model Measurement of Productive Biological Assets</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Depreciating an orchard over its productive life</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: An apple orchard</div><div class="wk-body">A company plants an apple orchard at a cost of RMB 6,000,000, with an estimated 20-year productive life once mature, and no active market evidence available for a reliable fair value.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company applies the COST MODEL, depreciating the orchard OVER its 20-year PRODUCTIVE life: RMB 6,000,000 ÷ 20 = <strong>RMB 300,000 per year</strong> — REFLECTING the SAME cost-based APPROACH applied to FIXED assets, RATHER than fair VALUE remeasurement each PERIOD.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Worked Example — a Rare Fair Value Election</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A narrow case where an active market genuinely exists</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A commodity with a transparent, active spot market</div><div class="wk-body">A company holds a consumable biological asset (a specific grain crop) traded on a genuinely active, transparent domestic commodity exchange with frequent, reliable spot prices.</div><div class="wk-answer">GIVEN the CLEAR active-market evidence, the company MAY ELECT the FAIR VALUE model for THIS asset — measuring it at FAIR VALUE LESS costs to SELL each period — though this REMAINS a NARROW EXCEPTION relative to the OVERWHELMING majority of Chinese biological ASSETS measured at COST.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 5 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Classification of biological assets (consumable, productive, public welfare)</span><span>Measurement model applied, and the basis for any fair value election</span><span>Depreciation method and useful life, for productive biological assets</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Correctly classifying a biological asset among the three categories</span><span>Whether sufficiently reliable active-market evidence exists to justify the fair value model</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Productive useful life and depreciation method for productive biological assets</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 41</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 5 vs IAS 41</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 5</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 41</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Default measurement basis</span><span>COST — fair value is the exception</span><span>FAIR VALUE less costs to sell — cost is the exception</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A DIRECTLY REVERSED presumption — ARGUABLY the SINGLE clearest EXAMPLE, across the ENTIRE ASBE suite, of China TAKING the OPPOSITE starting POINT from its OWN internationally-converged COUNTERPART standard.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every biological asset event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Depreciation (productive biological assets)</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Systematic, over the productive useful life</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Transfer to inventory (consumable, at harvest)</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span></span><span>Governed thereafter by ASBE No. 1</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 1</span><span>Inventories — consumable biological assets transfer here upon harvest or sale</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 4</span><span>Fixed Assets — supplies the same cost-model depreciation mechanics applied to productive biological assets</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s16"><span class="num">16</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Productive biological asset</div><div class="glossary-def">A living animal or plant held to produce agricultural output repeatedly or continuously (e.g. fruit trees, dairy cattle), depreciated like a fixed asset.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Consumable biological asset</div><div class="glossary-def">A living animal or plant held for eventual harvest or sale, measured at cost until transferred to inventory.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bo">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
